{
  "abstract": "For every real ε > 0, there are finitely many nonnegative real  heights p₀,…,p_d, at least one positive, such that the autoconvolution  of the step function taking height pⱼ on [j,j+1) and zero elsewhere  has the ratio (L² norm)^2 / ((L¹ norm) (L∞ norm)) greater than 1−ε.",
